      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1060,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rT0br",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Capture · mobile",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V2fSju",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nAPPROVED and in code (photos-d39, 2026-09-27).\n1. PURPOSE\nStart a design in one screen, in the order a person thinks: what furniture, how big if they know, photos if they have them, and anything else in their own words.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nHome \"Nuevo diseño\" (src/ui/capture/Home.tsx). A failed design comes back here with everything kept. Home also offers \"O empieza de una base\" (Home.tsx, #139): a grid of bases drawn as line sketches (sketch.ts) with category chips past six bases; \"Capture / Home\" is the app as it is now. \"Start from a base\" is the 2026-09-28 proposal (photo-like cards, no tagline) and differs from what shipped: the owner decides which stands.\n3. SCREENS (columns are the steps, left → right; a step's states stack below it)\n- Home\n- One screen, no expert connected: the banner first, with \"Conectar experto\" and \"Probar con los ejemplos simulados\"; neutral, not amber (K6)\n- One screen, empty: kind undecided, no measures, no photos; the description is the way in (\"Diseñar sin fotos\")\n- One screen, filled: Librero chosen, typical measures added and editable, 3 photos (one still being read), a note\n- Analyzing\n4. BUSINESS RULES\n- Measures are optional. \"Agregar medidas\" fills the kind's typical measures (NEW: a table per kind; only tables have one today, TYPICAL_TABLE_DIMENSIONS). Changing the kind before touching them re-fills them.\n- Without a kind, \"Agregar medidas\" starts from 600 × 1800 × 300, today's default.\n- One \"Agregar fotos\", up to 5, camera or gallery; each photo is read when added and the model labels its view; the person fixes the label if wrong (D39).\n- No required photos, and the expert no longer asks for photos in the chat (D39 amended 2026-09-27).\n- A photo's note stays open as a text field while it has text: closing it on blur moved \"Analizar\" under the pointer and lost the click (UI-8).\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/capture/Capture.tsx, src/ui/system/KindSelect.tsx. NEW: \"¿Qué mueble quieres?\", \"Agregar medidas\", \"Sin medidas\" (removes them), \"Típicas de un librero; cámbialas si ya mediste el tuyo.\", \"Fotos\", \"Agregar fotos\", \"hasta 5\", \"3 de 5\", \"Agregar una nota\", \"Mirando la foto…\". Thumbnails are 3D renders standing in for photos.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nDark mode (the tokens carry it). Every other state is in the states band below.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-7, UI-8, UI-19 · D39\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "R2AsWT",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7339,
      "name": "BRIEF — Capture · desktop",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 420,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lU5iK",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Capture · desktop",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s8Zle",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-30\n1. PURPOSE\nStart a design in one of two ways (UI-29): pick a ready-made base and adjust it at once, without an expert; or describe a piece of furniture (photos, words, the rough space) with an optional expert the person connects with their own key. The bases never need the expert.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nOpening the app with no design.\n3. SCREENS (columns are the steps; every screen here is a proposal, except the last one of step 3)\n- Step 1 · Home: Catalog first (no expert), Catalog first with an expert connected, and a category with few bases. The bases are the hero (nine tiles, stable order per session, \"Destacados\"; two are placeholders, there are seven fichas); the custom path is a named door in the hero, \"Diseña el tuyo\", whose button is primary only with an expert and \"Conectar experto\" in secondary otherwise (UI-31); the last tile of every list is \"¿No está el tuyo?\". The header carries the expert's status and Ajustes; the footer says where designs live.\n- Step 2 · Adjust your base (the bases path; proposal, UI-29): after choosing a base, before the Studio, a short step with the base's 3D and only the questions its ficha allows: where it will go (the space in cm, optional, the base's own measures shown as the starting point), what it holds (counters for what the ficha says can change: drawers, doors, open niches for this sideboard; each base shows its own, for example shelves and doors for the shoe rack, drawers for the bed), and the finish; a live summary of sheets and approximate cost; \"Abrir en el Studio\" and \"Saltar y usar la base tal cual\". NEW strings: \"¿Dónde lo vas a poner?\", \"¿Qué lleva?\", \"¿Cómo lo quieres?\", \"Lo que se puede cambiar lo dice la ficha de este mueble.\", \"Abrir en el Studio\", \"Saltar y usar la base tal cual\". Open: that the questions come from the ficha is a design decision the code does not have yet (today the plan sheet lists every field of the module), and so are the limits of each counter.\n- Step 3 · Connect the expert: the step over the dimmed Home, opened from \"Conectar experto\" or the header pill; and its state when a key is already saved (\"Tus llaves están guardadas\": use it or \"Usar una llave nueva\"). The passphrase is optional: with it the key is saved encrypted, without it the key lasts the tab. No \"where to get a key\" path for now.\n- Step 4 · Describe your furniture: without an expert (a banner and \"Conectar experto\" as the button), empty (\"Describe tu mueble o agrega una foto\" on the disabled button), ready (\"Diseñar mi mueble\"). Kind, description, the space in cm, photos, a way back to the bases. With photos: the description's label becomes \"¿Algo que el experto deba saber?\" (the code's wording when there are photos) with an optional hint (NEW), the photos are the code's tiles (view, note, read state), and the button stays \"Diseñar mi mueble\".\n- Step 5 · Analyzing: the original sketch and stages, the clock under the sketch, a history of real steps in a footer that fades upward.\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nThe main button of the custom path is disabled until there are 15 characters or a photo (Capture.tsx); the space is asked in cm and the code takes mm today; each photo is read when added.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/capture/{Home,Capture,Analyzing}.tsx, src/ui/settings/{Settings,Keys}.tsx, src/ports/Preferences.ts (PRESETS). NEW strings, not in code: the Home headline and its door (\"Elige un mueble. Ajústalo. Ármalo tú mismo.\", \"Diseña el tuyo\", \"¿No está el tuyo?\", \"Destacados\", the count line), the header and footer notes, \"Conecta tu experto\" with its sub-line and \"Conectar\", the form's sub-line, the space section, the disabled-button labels and the expert-decides wording (\"Que el experto lo decida\").\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nThe mobile band applies as is. Not drawn: reading failed and design failed (they wait in the mobile \"To review\" column), the correcting state of Analyzing and the end that opens the Studio, and the motion (the turn of the sketches, the fade and scroll of the history).\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-29, UI-30, UI-31, UI-32, UI-35\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
